# Development only.
#
# Three local servers, and picking the wrong one produces an error that looks
# like a backend or database fault rather than a configuration mistake:
#
#   5173  this app's dev server           (npm run dev)
#   8001  the EID Django API              (python manage.py runserver 8001)
#   8000  the identity provider           (serves /o/... and /auth/... only)
#
# Port 8000 is not the dashboard API: /api/health/, /api/expenses/ and
# /api/auth/me/ all answer 404 there. Pointing VITE_API_URL at 8000 therefore
# makes every data request fail in a way that reads like a database outage.
#
# Never start the backend with a bare `runserver`. That defaults to 8000, and
# Django on Windows sets allow_reuse_address, so it binds the port that the
# identity provider already holds without any "address already in use" error.
# It then receives no traffic at all, because every connection goes to whoever
# bound the port first. Always pass the port explicitly.
#
# The Vite proxy in vite.config.ts must name the same backend; a proxy that
# still reaches the deployed server while these variables reach the local one
# sends half the traffic to each, which is what produced a sign-in that worked
# and then started answering "Sign-in could not be started. Please try again."
#
# Production builds ignore this file and use `.env.production`, which sets
# /api; nginx proxies that to the backend in the deployed container.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8001/api
VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:8001/api

# The identity provider, used only to sign out (see signOutUrl in
# src/lib/api/core.ts). Signing *in* is handled by the backend, which redirects
# to whichever provider its GREENHILL_OIDC_DISCOVERY_URL names — locally that
# is http://127.0.0.1:8000, so the session that has to be ended is the one on
# this local provider too. A deployed URL here would end a different account's
# session and leave the local one signed in, so sign-out would appear to do
# nothing and the next sign-in would not ask for a password.
VITE_SSO_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000